#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0322 expect=violation domain=ADEFF
#note "TWO columns match ^TRTPG(\\d+)$, so the expander emits two concrete rules (y=1 and y=2) and the harness aggregates their violations. The y=1 rule fires once (row 3, TRTPG1 minority within DrugA); the y=2 rule fires once (row 6, TRTPG2 minority within DrugB). Pin on multi-expansion aggregation."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#expectViolationCount 2
#expectViolationAt row=3 TRTPG1=POOL2 TRTP=DrugA
#expectViolationAt row=6 TRTPG2=MID TRTP=DrugB
dataset ADEFF
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col TRTP    type=Char
col TRTPG1  type=Char
col TRTPG2  type=Char
---
S1 | 001 | DrugA | POOL1 | HIGH
S1 | 002 | DrugA | POOL1 | HIGH
S1 | 003 | DrugA | POOL2 | HIGH
S1 | 004 | DrugB | POOLX | LOW
S1 | 005 | DrugB | POOLX | LOW
S1 | 006 | DrugB | POOLX | MID
